# Copy to .env for local integration-test runs, then fill in the license key.
# .env is gitignored — never commit real key values.
#
# Format is godotenv-compatible: KEY=value, no `export` prefix, no shell quoting.
# The integration test helper loads it via github.com/joho/godotenv, which does
# not override variables already set in the environment.
#
# To copy the key from the conductor repo:
#   grep CONDUCTOR_LOCAL_LICENSE_KEY ~/conductor/.env \
#     | sed -E 's/^(export )?CONDUCTOR_LOCAL_LICENSE_KEY=/DBOS_CONDUCTOR_LICENSE_KEY=/' >> .env
#
# In CI this comes from the GitHub Actions secret CONDUCTOR_LOCAL_LICENSE_KEY,
# reusing the name conductor's own workflows use.

# Conductor license key. Conductor panics at startup without it
# (~/conductor/config/config.go:206). Use the *local* key: its hash is
# hardcoded in conductor's localKeyHashes, so validation happens offline. Any
# other key forces a license-server network call on every container boot.
DBOS_CONDUCTOR_LICENSE_KEY=

# Conductor source for the integration test. No location is assumed: with
# neither of these set, the integration test fails. Provide one:
#   CONDUCTOR_DIR   - path to a local conductor checkout; built via its
#                     docker/Dockerfile. Required today (no published image has
#                     the API yet).
#   CONDUCTOR_IMAGE - a conductor image tag that includes the API. Preferred
#                     once such an image exists.
CONDUCTOR_DIR=
# CONDUCTOR_IMAGE=
